        "contact": {
            "title": "Contact",
            "text": "<p>We are happy to answer your technical questions about our model of the city of Gelsenkirchen.<br><br><strong>Please contact us:</strong><br> City of Gelsenkirchen<br> Department 62 Surveying and Cadastre<br> Goldbergstraße 12<br> 45894 Gelsenkirchen<br><br> Holger Herrmann<br><br> Phone +49 (209) 169-4573<br><a href='mailto:geodaten@gelsenkirchen.de'>geodaten@gelsenkirchen.de</a><br><br> For content-related questions about geodata or thematic maps of the city of Gelsenkirchen, please contact the contact persons of the data provider. You can find your respective contact persons under metadata behind the data sources link.</p>"
        },
        "information": {
            "title": "Information",
            "text": "<p>The 3D city model Gelsenkirchen provides you with access to many three-dimensional datasets. The viewer starts with a preselection of these contents. Preloaded you will find, for example, 3D buildings (existing and planned), bridges, trees and the terrain model. Additional 2D data such as the city boundary and the web map complement the display. Furthermore, WMS services and own datasets can be loaded or displayed 3D objects can be hidden individually or as a whole. In addition to pure visualization, the 3D city model also offers analysis and interaction possibilities, such as visibility analysis or various measurement tools.</p><h3><b>Current Version: 1.4.6</b></h3><div><b>Version 1.4.6</b><ul><li>converted compass and inspector to web components</li><li>general bugfixes</li></ul></div><b>Version: 1.4.5</b><div><ul><li>Improved visibility analysis</li><li>Improved water level analysis</li><li>Animated water bodies and water level analysis</li><li>Temporary: Christmas tree on the Nordsternturm. Merry Christmas!</li></ul></div>"
        },
